<title>UK: Arjo Wiggins to shed 160 jobs in the U.S..</title>
<headline>Arjo Wiggins to shed 160 jobs in the U.S..</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Appleton Papers Inc, the main U.S. subsidiary of British paper manufacturer Arjo Wiggins Appleton Plc, said on Tuesday it was planning to close down certain older and less cost-effective equipment at its Newton Falls mill.</p>
<p>The closure would result in loss of 160 jobs, the company said.  </p>
<p>The company said the closure was part of its efforts to improve its position in America's coated free sheet paper market in which it made its debut in June 1995.</p>
<p>Arjo bought the Newton Falls mill in New York and began expansion of is Combined Locks facility in Wisconsin. Total investment in these projects was $210 million stg.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
